{:tier :glm-5.2, :verse 23, :comments ["And he said to them: That which YHWH spoke — from the first day onward I did not tell you. And Moshe intended that they would be astonished when they found a double portion, to make known to them now the honor of the Sabbath day." "Bake — it should have been אֱפֵה with hatef-patah qatan, like from אכל comes אֱכֹל, from אמר comes אֱמֹר, from אפה comes אֱפֵה — imperative form. But because it is not in construct with what follows, rather it carries the revia‘ accent, which is one of the accents of kings, therefore it is pointed with tsere. And I have found no parallel for it except הֵבוּ: אהבו הבו קלון מגניה (Hosea 4:18)."], :book :exodus, :voice :rashbam, :lang :en, :chapter 16, :notes {1 "The lemma reflects the single word אפוּ ('bake it') at the end of the verse; the discussion concerns the unexpected vowel pointing of this imperative form."}, :source-witnesses [{"versionTitle" "Sefaria community Hebrew (PD)", "language" "he"}], :timestamp "2026-07-30T14:41:48.701252032Z", :translated-from :he, :model "glm-5.2"}